$\begin{align}
\text{vertex's }t\text{-coordinate}&=\dfrac{(\goldD{4})+(\goldD{-8})}{2}
\\\\
&=\blueD{-2}
\end{align}$

Now we can find the vertex's $y$-coordinate by evaluating $h(\blueD{-2})$:

$\begin{align}
h(\blueD{-2})&=(\blueD{-2}-4)(\blueD{-2}+8)
\\\\
&=(-6)(6)
\\\\
&=-36
\end{align}$
